# ---- HOST-NATIVE STATION (de-bridged 2026-08-12, conversion campaign) ----
# The SAME host-native bbcb binary shape as bbcmicro, with the ARM second
# processor in the Tube, the 1770 disc interface, ADFS 1.30 in socket 3 and
# Disc 3 in the drive. Launcher: shared stations/mame-native/x11-runtime.sh;
# reset = relaunch restoring the golden savestate (which carries the baked
# "A* *LIB $" / "A* AB" supervisor lines the fixture documents).
SH_RESET_MODE=relaunch
SH_FIXTURE_DESC=Acorn ARM Evaluation System (1986) — the first ARM product ever sold — sitting at the prompt of ARM BBC Basic V version 1.00, running ON the ARM second processor. The screen reads "ARM Second Processor 4096K / Acorn ADFS / BASIC", then the two supervisor lines that got it there, "A* *LIB $" and "A* AB", then the ARM BASIC banner and a ">" prompt. Those two A* lines are BAKED INTO the golden savestate, not typed by a visitor: the board has no operating system of its own, the language comes off Disc 3 as $.AB, and the ADFS library is "Unset" on a cold boot so *LIB $ is required before AB resolves. Drawn by MAME 0.289's bbcb running HOST-NATIVE (drawshm) with -tube arm, the Acorn 1770 disc interface (the .adl discs are double density; the 8271 cannot read them) and ADFS 1.30 in sideways socket 3 — socket 1 kills the Tube outright. Published surface 800x600; -artwork_crop removes the keyboard-LED strip. The frame is black, white, and the pure #0000FF of the reverse-video A* field. CAPS LOCK is on at reset. Keyboard-only exhibit; no pointer device; sound -> FIFO.
MAME_NATIVE_BIN=/data/vms/streamhost/assets/armeval/mame-native/bbcb
MAME_NATIVE_DRIVER=bbcb
MAME_NATIVE_ROMS=/data/vms/streamhost/assets/armeval/mame-native/roms
MAME_NATIVE_GEOM=800x600
MAME_NATIVE_ARGS=-tube arm -fdc acorn1770 -rom3 /data/vms/streamhost/assets/armeval/mame-native/media/Acorn-ADFS-1.30.rom -flop1 /data/vms/streamhost/assets/armeval/mame-native/media/armevaluationsystem-disc3.adl -artwork_crop
MAME_NATIVE_SKIP_WARNINGS=1
SH_MAMECTL_SOCK=/data/vms/streamhost/stations/armeval/ctl.sock
SH_MAMESOCK_KEYMAP=/data/vms/streamhost/stations/armeval/armeval.keymap
SH_AUDIO_SOURCE=fifo
SH_AUDIO_FIFO=/data/vms/streamhost/stations/armeval/audio.fifo

# ---- KEYBOARD PACING (the exhibit's only input surface) ----
SH_KEY_MIN_HOLD_MS=80
SH_KEY_MIN_GAP_MS=80
SH_KEY_MAP=":@,':&,&:^,(:*,):(,=:_,@:\,+:%3A,^:=,~:+,_:`,%3A:',*:"
